\title{ezrmodel: Single-Line Modelling and Clustering for Consumer Data}
\description{
Turns the advanced-analytics tasks that research and insights professionals reach for into single-line helpers that return a complete, diagnosable result. Find what drives a target variable (a consensus of correlation, regression, relative-weights, random-forest and factor importance), segment data with clustering and read off the diagnostics and cluster profiles, reduce dimensions, fit and tidy regressions, and run grouped hypothesis tests. Designed around a session 'default dataset' so the same pattern works across surveys, social and ecommerce data. Also turns open text into tidy term frequencies, tf-idf, topic models and extractive summaries, and checks latent structure with scale reliability, exploratory factor analysis and confirmatory models. Selects predictors with stepwise or penalised regression, compares fitted models on common metrics, and embeds data in two dimensions with UMAP or t-SNE.
